cff-version: 1.2.0
title: RTL8852CE Bluetooth/Wi-Fi Coexistence Toolkit for Linux
message: >-
  If you use this work in your research, debugging, or derivative
  patches, please cite it using this metadata.
authors:
  - family-names: Gouda
    given-names: Hamza
    email: hraafat357@gmail.com
version: 1.1.1
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/hamza-gouda1/rtl8852ce-bt-coex"
abstract: >-
  Instrumented rtw89 driver patches, a correlated capture harness, and
  repair tooling for the Realtek RTL8852CE combo card on Linux. Firmware
  version mismatch, an empty Wi-Fi-side AFH report and rejected mailbox
  messages on one ASUS laptop strongly indicate a coexistence problem.
  The toolkit includes a direct-HCI AFH workaround, live policy tuning,
  verified sends, live-map readback, a hold-down against Wi-Fi flaps,
  measurement tooling for the Bluetooth-to-Wi-Fi direction and an AFH
  positive control. The workaround was validated on one laptop. A controlled
  rerun produced zero measured Wi-Fi overlap under both host classifications,
  so it could not isolate the guard's independent effect.
keywords:
  - linux
  - bluetooth
  - wifi
  - rtw89
  - realtek
  - coexistence
  - a2dp
  - kernel
